# evidence-for: AC-018, AC-019, AC-020
# evidence-volatile: Installed \d+ packages? in \d+(\.\d+)?ms
# evidence-timeout: 120
#
# SCOPE BOUNDARY RECORD — NOT an implementation claim.
#
# AC-018 (Foundry-Stream accepts the reconciled stream ids), AC-019
# (Foundry-Defect / Foundry-Sync accept type PARTIAL) and AC-020 (per-cycle
# PROVE tranche accumulation) are cited in casting 4's <spec_requirements>
# because they are siblings of AC-021 under US-006 — one story, four criteria.
# Casting 4's Requirement Classification assigns only AC-021 to this casting
# and states of the other three: "AC-018, AC-019 and AC-020 within it belong
# to castings 2 and 3, and are here as context for the whole story, not as
# work for you."
#
# This file binds those three IDs so the acceptance gate's coverage pass has
# an explicit, re-executable record of WHERE they are not, rather than an
# unexplained gap. The command lists every callable DEFINED IN
# foundry_spawn.py — casting 4's only source file. The complete public
# surface is three entry points:
#
#   foundry_cast_wave        bulk spawn  (FR-020 / AC-025 fix lands here)
#   foundry_liveness         NEW, FR-015 / AC-021 / CT-004
#   foundry_spawn_teammate   single spawn (FR-015 protocol block lands here)
#
# There is no foundry_mark_stream, no foundry_defect, no foundry_sync and no
# coverage roll-up handler in this module, and casting 4 is forbidden from
# editing the modules that hold them (foundry_orchestrator.py, server.py,
# schemas/vocab.py). Evidence that AC-018/AC-019/AC-020 are SATISFIED belongs
# to castings 2 and 3 under their own commits.
#
# GRIND cycle 5 (D-058) adds three PRIVATE helpers to the list below —
# _with_dispatch, _latest_teammate_dispatches, _missing_teammate_records — and
# no new entry point. The public surface is still the three tools above, so
# the boundary this file records is unchanged.
#
# TEMPER cycle 6 (D-115) adds one more PRIVATE helper — _manifest_shape_error,
# the shared wrong-typed-manifest refusal both spawn doors call — and again no
# new entry point. D-114 and D-117 changed only the bodies of
# _agent_liveness_record and foundry_liveness, so they add no name at all. The
# boundary is still the same three tools.
# GRIND cycle 19 (D-132) adds two more PRIVATE helpers — _shape_problem, the
# recursive walker over a declared shape, and _manifest_shape_problem, the
# string half both TOLERANT readers consult so they degrade on exactly the
# evidence the two doors refuse on. _manifest_shape_error keeps its name and
# its role as the refusal envelope. The module also grows two non-callable
# module constants that do not appear below: _MANIFEST_SHAPE (the declared
# structure) and _REQUIRED (its present-and-non-null sentinel).
#
# Still no new entry point. The public surface is the same three tools, and the
# boundary this file records is unchanged.
#
